---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="Agent Workflow Atlas - SuperAda" description="A public-safe atlas of 100 receipt-backed Enterprise Crew workflows across nine agents and twelve operating categories." />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main class="workflow-atlas">
      <section class="atlas-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow">SuperAda Field Guide</p>
        <h1>What an AI crew can do when every action leaves a receipt.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Browse the public-safe version of our v1 operating atlas: 100 workflow loops across research, communication, software, fleet work, content, business intelligence, media, governance, and personal support. The private proof ledger stays private; the reusable pattern and approval boundary are published.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="#catalog">Browse the catalog</a>
          <a href="#recipes" class="secondary">Copy a recipe</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="stat-grid" aria-label="Atlas summary">
        {stats.map((stat) => <article><span>{stat.label}</span><strong>{stat.value}</strong></article>)}
      </section>

      <section class="notice">
        <strong>Public edition.</strong> Internal proof links, private task URLs, customer/contact names, and raw source excerpts are not exposed here. Verified means the private ledger has a receipt. Inferred means the row is useful but still needs a direct public-safe receipt before it should be treated as proven.
      </section>

      <section class="visuals" aria-labelledby="visuals-title">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Rich media map</p>
          <h2 id="visuals-title">Five visual primitives for the operating system</h2>
          <p>The diagrams show how the catalog works without leaking the underlying private receipts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="visual-grid">
          {atlas.visuals.map((visual) => (
            <figure>
              <img src={visual.src} alt={visual.title} loading="lazy" />
              <figcaption>{visual.title}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="categories" class="categories" aria-labelledby="categories-title">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Twelve lanes</p>
          <h2 id="categories-title">Start with the operating lane</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="category-grid">
          {atlas.categories.map((category) => (
            <article>
              <span>{category.id}</span>
              <h3>{category.name}</h3>
              <p>{category.promise}</p>
              <small>{category.visual_primitive}</small>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="recipes" class="recipes" aria-labelledby="recipes-title">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Copyable loops</p>
          <h2 id="recipes-title">Recipes, not magic prompts</h2>
          <p>Replace the inputs. Keep the proof step. Do not remove the gate. Stunningly annoying how often that last bit saves everyone. 💀</p>
        </div>
        <div class="recipe-grid">
          <article><h3>Call transcript → tracked commitments</h3><p>Extract only explicit commitments. Return owner, due date, source quote or location, duplicate check, and whether it needs human approval. Do not send messages.</p><small>Gate: external follow-up requires approval.</small></article>
          <article><h3>Question → cited evidence dossier</h3><p>Answer from sources. Keep observations, inferences, and recommendations separate. Cite every material claim and name missing proof.</p><small>Gate: research and local drafting are autonomous.</small></article>
          <article><h3>Evidence bundle → public draft</h3><p>Turn evidence into a channel-ready draft. Preserve citations. Return a claim sheet and stop before publishing.</p><small>Gate: public delivery requires approval.</small></article>
          <article><h3>Validated task → bounded coding candidate</h3><p>Implement in an isolated worktree. Stay in scope. Run exact gates and return receipts, not vibes wearing a lab coat.</p><small>Gate: merge, push, deploy, and release are separate.</small></article>
          <article><h3>Health signal → reversible fleet repair</h3><p>Diagnose the live route first. Snapshot before change. Apply the smallest safe repair, then smoke-test and record before/after evidence.</p><small>Gate: destructive or critical-access actions need approval.</small></article>
          <article><h3>Daily metrics → decision pack</h3><p>Show period, denominator, revenue, cost, profit, risk, and recommended action in one view.</p><small>Gate: budget or commercial changes need approval.</small></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="catalog" class="catalog" aria-labelledby="catalog-title">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">100 public-safe workflow rows</p>
          <h2 id="catalog-title">Filter by agent, risk, proof, or lane</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="filters" aria-label="Catalog filters">
          <input id="atlas-search" type="search" placeholder="Search category, agent, risk, input, or tool path" />
          <select id="agent-filter"><option value="">All agents</option>{atlas.agents.map((agent) => <option value={agent}>{agent}</option>)}</select>
          <select id="proof-filter"><option value="">All proof states</option><option>Verified</option><option>Inferred</option></select>
        </div>
        <p id="catalog-count" class="count">100 workflows shown</p>
        <div class="workflow-grid" id="workflow-grid">
          {atlas.rows.map((row) => (
            <article class="workflow-card" data-search={`${row.id} ${row.category} ${row.agents.join(' ')} ${row.evidence} ${row.risk} ${row.inputs} ${row.toolPath}`.toLowerCase()} data-agents={row.agents.join('|')} data-proof={row.evidence}>
              <div class="card-top"><span>{row.id}</span><strong>{row.evidence}</strong></div>
              <h3>{row.category}</h3>
              <p>{row.toolPath}</p>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>Agents</dt><dd>{row.agents.join(', ')}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Inputs</dt><dd>{row.inputs || 'Declared sources'}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Risk</dt><dd>{row.risk}</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <small>{row.approval}</small>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="video" aria-labelledby="video-title">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Script-to-video runway</p>
          <h2 id="video-title">Three production treatments ready for rendering</h2>
          <p>The v1 release includes storyboards and motion contracts. Final generated video is a separate production pass so exact labels and continuity can be verified frame by frame.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="video-grid">
          {atlas.videoTreatments.map((treatment) => <article><span>{treatment.duration}</span><h3>{treatment.title}</h3><p>{treatment.cta}</p></article>)}
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
    <script>
      const search = document.getElementById('atlas-search') as HTMLInputElement | null;
      const agent = document.getElementById('agent-filter') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
      const proof = document.getElementById('proof-filter') as HTMLSelectElement | null;
      const cards = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.workflow-card'));
      const count = document.getElementById('catalog-count');
      function applyFilters() {
        const q = (search?.value || '').trim().toLowerCase();
        const selectedAgent = agent?.value || '';
        const selectedProof = proof?.value || '';
        let visible = 0;
        cards.forEach((card) => {
          const haystack = card.dataset.search || '';
          const agents = card.dataset.agents || '';
          const proofState = card.dataset.proof || '';
          const show = (!q || haystack.includes(q)) && (!selectedAgent || agents.split('|').includes(selectedAgent)) && (!selectedProof || proofState === selectedProof);
          card.hidden = !show;
          if (show) visible += 1;
        });
        if (count) count.textContent = `${visible} workflows shown`;
      }
      [search, agent, proof].forEach((el) => el?.addEventListener('input', applyFilters));
    </script>
    <style>
      .workflow-atlas { width:min(1180px, calc(100% - 32px)); margin:0 auto; padding:56px 0 80px; }
      .atlas-hero { border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:36px; padding:clamp(28px, 6vw, 72px); background:radial-gradient(circle at top left, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent), transparent 36%), linear-gradient(135deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 92%, transparent), color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 95%, transparent)); box-shadow:0 30px 90px color-mix(in srgb, var(--glow) 18%, transparent); }
      .eyebrow { color:var(--accent); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.18em; font-size:12px; font-weight:900; margin:0 0 14px; }
      h1 { max-width:980px; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:clamp(46px, 8vw, 96px); line-height:.93; letter-spacing:-.055em; margin:0; }
      .lede { max-width:820px; color:var(--muted); font-size:clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 23px); line-height:1.55; margin:28px 0 0; }
      .hero-actions { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin-top:30px; }
      .hero-actions a { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; min-height:48px; padding:0 18px; border-radius:999px; background:var(--accent); color:#120b04; font-weight:900; text-decoration:none; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.08em; font-size:12px; }
      .hero-actions a.secondary { background:transparent; color:var(--text); border:1px solid var(--border); }
      .stat-grid, .category-grid, .recipe-grid, .video-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr)); gap:14px; margin-top:18px; }
      .stat-grid article, .category-grid article, .recipe-grid article, .video-grid article, .workflow-card, .notice { border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:24px; background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 84%, transparent); padding:20px; }
      .stat-grid article span, .category-grid article span, .video-grid article span { color:var(--accent); font-size:12px; font-weight:900; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; }
      .stat-grid article strong { display:block; font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:44px; margin-top:8px; }
      .notice { margin:18px 0 52px; color:var(--muted); line-height:1.7; }
      .notice strong { color:var(--text); }
      section { margin-top:64px; }
      .section-head { max-width:780px; margin-bottom:22px; }
      .section-head h2 { font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,58px); line-height:1; letter-spacing:-.04em; margin:0; }
      .section-head p:not(.eyebrow) { color:var(--muted); line-height:1.65; }
      .visual-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr)); gap:18px; }
      figure { margin:0; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:24px; padding:12px; background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 70%, transparent); }
      figure img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; border-radius:16px; background:#071018; }
      figcaption { margin:10px 4px 2px; color:var(--muted); font-weight:800; }
      .category-grid h3, .recipe-grid h3, .video-grid h3, .workflow-card h3 { margin:10px 0; font-size:20px; }
      .category-grid p, .recipe-grid p, .video-grid p, .workflow-card p, .workflow-card small, .category-grid small, .recipe-grid small { color:var(--muted); line-height:1.55; }
      .filters { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 170px 170px; gap:12px; margin:18px 0 10px; }
      .filters input, .filters select { min-height:48px; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:14px; background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 78%, transparent); color:var(--text); padding:0 14px; }
      .count { color:var(--muted); font-weight:800; }
      .workflow-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(290px,1fr)); gap:14px; }
      .card-top { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:12px; }
      .card-top span, .card-top strong { color:var(--accent); font-size:12px; font-weight:900; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; }
      .workflow-card dl { display:grid; gap:8px; margin:16px 0; }
      .workflow-card div { min-width:0; }
      .workflow-card dt { color:var(--accent); font-size:11px; font-weight:900; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.12em; }
      .workflow-card dd { margin:2px 0 0; color:var(--text); overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
      @media (max-width:720px) { .workflow-atlas { width:min(100% - 24px, 1180px); padding-top:28px; } .filters { grid-template-columns:1fr; } h1 { font-size:48px; } .atlas-hero { border-radius:26px; } }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
